        "id": 1265046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-22T07:08:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "IMHO, while(1) is not good here. If the i2c read failed, for example the EEPROM was broken, this loop will never exit. Moreover, the AP may be powered on during i2c read failed, the wrong EDID may be read by AP, continue trying to read/write is meaningless.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "cf487f028d9aaaec203e6d131cf4a7042f5397d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "26834c29_64f5ae63",
        "filename": "board/karma/panel.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1267183
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-22T09:43:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In our opinion currently, if EDID is out of control, we would rather machine can not power-on.\nIf you think this loop should exit when i2c_read keeps failed, could you suggest retry times for this case?",
      "parentUuid": "2be1e41a_5c2e00c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "cf487f028d9aaaec203e6d131cf4a7042f5397d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8afc1dc3_d44f51c0",
        "filename": "board/karma/panel.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1265046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-23T11:41:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Maybe you can just output the error message instead of while(1). Without the correct EDID, can the display output correctly? If not, we maybe can add a led state to indicate this kind of error to speed up the debugging/RMA process. Just my two cents.",
      "parentUuid": "26834c29_64f5ae63",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "cf487f028d9aaaec203e6d131cf4a7042f5397d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bdcd0db4_cb1badde",
        "filename": "board/karma/panel.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1186994
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-11-26T12:20:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[1] When I2C slave is busy, it can reject host command. All you have to do is do it again later. Therefore, it is better to give a retry. Adding while(1) or not depends on the action after wrong EDID. (no infinite loop if decide to power on, infinite loop/retry/no retry if decide to stay power off)\n\n[2] Without the correct EDID, there might be nothing on your screen (I am  more tend to assume unknown fail will happen). EDID is important information for panel signals. It should be correct.\n\n[3] I am OK with LED as long as you have spec. for it.",
      "parentUuid": "8afc1dc3_d44f51c0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 62,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "cf487f028d9aaaec203e6d131cf4a7042f5397d5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
